   TUT Wuri Handayani; RISTEK BRIN},
Abstract = {This research was conducted to preserve some of the oral literature one
   of Folklore study, namely prohibited speech act in order not to
   disappear in people's life and still be preserved well by the community.
   Especially in Minang community in Ujungbatu area of Rokan Hulu, Riau.
   The purpose of this study is to describe the function of the speech
   utterances found in Ujungbatu area. The type of this research is
   qualitative study by using descriptive methods. The informants of this
   study were three Minang people who migrated to Ujungbatu. Data is
   collected through observation, interview, record and data recording
   techniques. Based on the findings and discussion, it was found speech
   abstinence prohibited in Minang community in area of Ujungbatu. This
   study describes the functions and meanings that exist in the prohibition
   speech, where the category is focused on the human life cycle and the
   categories found consist of: (1) as a thickening of religious emotions;
   2) the projected imagination a collective that comes from a person's
   hallucinations; 3) as an educational tool for children or adolescents;
   4) reasonable explanation.},
