Note = {2nd Advanced Research on Business, Management and Humanities (ARBUHUM),
   Phuket, THAILAND, OCT 10-12, 2017},
Organization = {Malaysia Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {Unsurprisingly, land use problems usually happened when there are
   significant changes which give the bad impact especially for the
   environment change. Land conversion occurred as well as the growth of
   socio-economic activities which require housing and better facilities.
   Land conversion often goes hand in hand with problems such as loss of
   farmland, food security problems, floods, landslides and other issues.
   The aim of this research is to identify the social capital impacts on
   land conversion. The object is land use around the national road of
   Pandaan which connects between Malang and Surabaya City of East Java,
   Indonesia. The high score of social capital depends on three variables,
   they are trust, social network and community participation. Data
   affiliation needed to measure the social capital through questionnaire
   survey towards total 203 respondents. The research used Structural
   Equation Modelling (SEM) and the result shows that trust variable obtain
   0,21, community participation on 0,08, social agreement and commitment
   variable equal to 0,53. It means that all of variables are on the
   positive value. The trust variable among them affects the community
   decision to sell their land.},
