   Voicila, Teodor-Iulian and Voiculescu, Daniel Iulian},
Book-Group-Author = {IEEE},
Title = {The Identification and Classification of Facial Expressions under Stress
   using an EMG},
Booktitle = {2021 INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON E-HEALTH AND BIOENGINEERING (EHB 2021),
   9TH EDITION},
Series = {E-Health and Bioengineering Conference},
Year = {2021},
Note = {9th IEEE International Conference on e-Health and Bioengineering (EHB),
   Grigore T Popa Univ Med \& Pharmacy, ELECTR NETWORK, NOV 18-19, 2021},
Organization = {IEEE; Grigore T Popa Univ Med \& Pharmacy, Fac Med Bioengineering; SRBM;
   IEEE Romanian Sect; IEEE EMB; IEEE Romania Sect; Inst Informatica
   Teoretica; Romanian Soc Med Bioengineering; Romanian Acad, Iasi Branch,
   Inst Comp Sci; IEEE EMB Romania Chapter; IEEE EMC Romania Chapter; IEEE
   Signal Proc Romania Chapter; IEEE SMC Romania Chapter},
Abstract = {Due to the growing number of people suffering from stroke or facial
   nerve damage which influence the quality of life, we propose an
   acquisition system that identify and classify facial expression by
   manual analysis of signals using an EMG. Beside these features, the
   designed system is able to save the records in a database so that these
   kinds of medical conditions can be seen when they first appeared and how
   they manifested along the way. The acquisition system has an interface
   created in MATLAB App Design, which facilitates the experience of signal
   acquisition and database creation. The signal acquisition occurred
   during the visual or auditory stimulation of four reactions, by means of
   videos made for this purpose. The extracted signals were manually
   segmented and analyzed. For that acquisition system, a cover was
   designed, and 3D printed, which has both a protective role and an
   aesthetic role. Although the paper investigates only a few facial
   expressions, it can be extended in the future to recognize emotions and
   even to make correlations between different facial expression and other
   medical conditions recorded in the database.},
