Year = {2010},
Pages = {210-213},
Note = {21st Pan-Asian Congress of Sports and Physical Education, Jiangxi Normal
   Univ, Nanchang, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 23-25, 2010},
Organization = {Pan Asian Soc Sports \& Phys Educ},
Abstract = {Based on stress theory, the relationship between coping styles, social
   support and burnout is discussed by means of questionnaire and
   mathematical statistics and analysis The purpose of this paper is to
   provide references to psychological education of athletic teams, improve
   training performance and to protect the physical and mental health of
   the athletes The findings indicate there is negative correlation between
   problems-focused coping and reduced sense of achievements and the former
   enters the regression equation for total score of burnout There is a
   significant positive correlation between avoidance coping transcendental
   coping and each factor of burnout and as well transcendental coping
   enters the regression equation for total score of burnout The social
   supports are important external ``buffers{''} in the stress process of
   elite athletes which have the largest effect on reduced sense of
   achievements factor of burnout, among which perceived family support
   plays the important role of intervening The more social supports may
   lead to more uses of positive coping styles such as problem-focused and
   emotion-focused coping by elite athletes to deal with the difficult
   situation},
