   \& Arts; Georgian Natl Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Turkish Acad Sci; Bulgarian Ind Assoc; Bulgarian Minist Environm \&
   Water},
Abstract = {Pollutants from the Bistrita river section Piatra Neamt Bacau, to the
   confluence with the river Siret, mainly derive from urban areas located
   along watercourse. These quantities of pollutants stack with the input
   from upstream areas of Piatra Neamt and smaller amounts are difficult to
   quantify because of diffuse sources and historical activities.
   Quantification of the influence of pollutants on Bistrita river factors
   affecting this section could be achieved by using a technical base of
   research that included the results of previous research on this body of
   water, its systematic monitoring activity and research in the field, as
   well as data collected from government statistical Siret water basin.
   The paper presents the variation of water quality indicators: oxygen
   dissolved, BOD5, COD-Cr, COD-Mn, ammonium, nitrate, nitrite and total
   phosphorus, monitored during 1970-2014 in Bistrita river sections:
   Piatra Neamt section; Roznov section; Frunzeni section; Piatra Neamt -
   Racova - Zanesti section; Garleni section; Recreational Lake downstream
   section; Downstream Bacau section.},
