Organization = {EUROPEAN ASSOC SCI AIR POLLUT; AEROSOL SOC; GESELL AEROSOLFORSCH; USA,
   EUROPEAN RES OFF},
Abstract = {Emission inventories show that diesel emissions are the main source of
   atmospheric particulate elemental carbon in Western Europe, contributing
   70-90\% of the national average and rising to more than 90\% in cities. 
   U.K. emissions are increasing at about 2 x 10(5) kg per annum.  The
   atmospheric concentration can be related to the areal emission rate by a
   model based on Gaussian diffusion theory.  Particulate elemental carbon
   is responsible for 30\% of the U.K. average dark smoke and 60\% of the
   dark smoke in London.  It is also a major contributor to the soiling of
   building surfaces.},
