Note = {Arab Management Conference, UNIV BRADFORD, BRADFORD, ENGLAND, JUL, 1993},
Abstract = {Expatriate and indigenous managers' perceptions of managerial problems
   in the United Arab Emirates (UAE) were compared. Problems were
   classified as subjective (personal) or objective (organizational and
   societal). Foreign expatriates scored significantly higher than Arab
   expatriates and indigenous managers on both subjective and objective
   problems. The major subjective problems were sensitivity to comments
   taken personally, weak inclination toward research and theory, and weak
   inner work incentives. Only two objective problems were identified:
   centralization of authority and inadequate planning and information
   systems.},
