   neurons that are tuned to stimulus features, then precisely what
   features are encoded and how do neurons in the system come to be
   sensitive to those features? Here we show differential responses to
   ripple stimuli can arise through exposure to formative stimuli in a
   recurrently connected model of the thalamocortical system which exhibits
   delays, lateral and recurrent connections, and learning in the form of
   spike timing dependent plasticity.},
