Abstract = {This study explored the interplay between young people's attitudes
   toward computer networks and Internet addiction. Ninety possible
   Internet addicts were selected for examination after analyzing the
   questionnaire responses of an initial sample of 753 Taiwanese high
   school adolescents. It was found that the subjects' attitudes toward
   computer networks could explain many aspects of Internet addiction.
   However, actual behaviors on Internet usage and perceptions on the
   usefulness of Internet were more important than affective responses
   toward computer networks in predicting adolescents' Internet addiction.},
