   Technologies for Coastal Area, Varna, BULGARIA, JUN 09-11, 2004},
Organization = {Bulgarian Natl Assoc Water; Int Water Assoc; European Water Assoc},
Abstract = {Sixteen sampling sites along the stream of Kamchia River were considered
   as environmental objects in the multivariate statistical study aimed to
   identify and apportion patterns of sampling sites, latent factors
   responsible for the data structure and their relation to the emitter
   industrial and anthropogenic sources in the vicinity of the sampling
   sites. As variables 11 surface water parameters monitored for a long
   time period (up to 11 years) were used. Four main site patterns were
   revealed by cluster analysis (urban, rural, near-to dam and estuary) and
   for each site latent factors were identified and apportioned (among them
   ``metallurgical{''}, ``food production{''}, ``winery{''}, domestic
   wastes{''}, ``natural{''}). The relative contribution of each identified
   pollution source to the formation of the total concentration of each
   chemical species or physicochemical parameter was determined and
   compared to the real emitters in the region of interest.},
