   AUG 04-07, 2004},
Organization = {Cognit Sci Soc},
Abstract = {CHREST (Chunk Hierarchy and REtrieval STructures) is a comprehensive,
   computational model of human learning and perception. It has been used
   to successfully simulate data in a variety of domains, including: the
   acquisition of syntactic categories ,expert behaviour, concept
   formation, implicit learning, and the acquisition of multiple
   representations in physics for problem solving. The aim of this tutorial
   is to provide participants with an introduction to CHREST, how it can be
   used to model various phenomena, and the knowledge to carry out their
   own modelling experiments.},
