   International-Society-for-Environmental-Information-Sciences on
   Environmental Informatics, Xiamen, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUL 26-28, 2005},
Organization = {Xiamen Univ; Ryerson Univ; Int Soc Environm Informat Sci},
Abstract = {In 2001, a project ``A comprehensive air quality management study for
   sustainable development in the City of Tangshan, China{''} was initiated
   aimed at developing effective air quality management strategies for
   improving air quality in Tangshan City. This paper presents the results
   from extensive data collection efforts conducted in this project. The
   comprehensive investigation of urban air quality and air pollutant
   emission in the study region are introduced. The obtained data have been
   used to address and tackle local air pollution problems and identify
   complex interactions among local geographical features, social and
   economic conditions, meteorological characters, emission sources,
   ambient air quality, and pollution meteorology. The results could
   provide useful information for the responsible authorities in
   determining which aspects of the air pollution problem are deemed most
   important and time critical by the decision makers. Some preliminary
   thoughts and discussions on making air quality management decisions
   presented at the end of this paper suggest that effective and efficient
   strategies should be pursued in setting future policy for improving air
   quality.},
