Note = {10th Asian Aerosol Conference (AAC), Korea Assoc Particle \& Aerosol
   Res, SOUTH KOREA, JUL 02-06, 2017},
Abstract = {This study investigated the magnetic capture of fine dust containing
   iron compounds using a metal mesh. Test filters were prepared by
   magnetizing stainless woven mesh with permanent magnetic bars. The iron
   content of the test dust was 8.66\%, 25.24\%, and 12\% for fly ash from
   a coal-fired power plant, effluent dust from a metro subway, and
   particulate matter from an urban integrated power plant boiler,
   respectively. Based on experimental results focusing on TSP, PM1, PM2.5,
   and PM2.5-10, the intensity of the source magnets is directly related to
   the dust capturing efficiency, and 7.41\% of additional subway dust can
   be collected with a source magnet of 3,000 gauss for structure of the
   dust was more effective for magnetic capture than the elemental iron
   composition. It was also found that the magnetized mesh filters
   contributed synergistically to improve the fine dust capture with low
   pressure resistance.},
