   Protection and Disaster Mitigation},
Year = {2004},
Pages = {349-356},
Note = {World Engineers Convention 2004, Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 02-06,
   2004},
Organization = {Shanghai Baosteel Grp Corp; Shanghai Automot Ind Corp; China Natl
   Petroleum Corp; China Petrochem Corp; State Grid Corp China; Shanghai
   Huizhong Automat Mfg Co Ltd; China Aerosp Sci \& Technol Corp; China
   Yangtze Three Gorges Project Dev Corp; China Natl Nucl Corp; BMW Grp
   Beijing; Chun Wo Construct \& Engn Co Ltd; Shui On Land Ltd; Air China},
Abstract = {A lot of vehicle technologies have been developed to improve air quality
   of urban area, fuel economy and decreasing CO2. Improvement of
   combustion and catalyst efficiency (catalyst itself and catalyst
   utilizing techniques (quick activation, accurate air fuel ratio
   control)) lead gasoline engines to satisfy strict California PZEV
   standard. On the other hand, decrease of NOx and PM of diesel engines
   was difficult because there was not an effective emission control
   technology. However, the new technique, which can decreases NOx and PM
   simultaneously has been developed recently. This state-of-the-art
   technique including accurate fuel injection control by common rail
   system enables to accomplish Euro4 emission regulation for diesel
   engines. However, because fuel quality has large influence on those
   technologies, it is essential to improve fuel quality in the market to
   improve air quality. Especially, decreasing sulfur and keeping
   cleanliness of fuel injectors and intake valves to enable accurate fuel
   injection control are important.},
