   2000},
Abstract = {The main contribution to helplessness research in Spain was on
   immunization against helplessness and how it was modulated by
   predictability in animals or attributions in humans. Recent research
   have focused on factors determining the perception of non-contingency
   during learned irrelevance and the illusion of control during an
   uncontrollable experience. Its subsequent effects on covariation
   learning and the detection of controllability showed the influence of
   prior beliefs and attentional factors on covariation learning and
   learned helplessness whose influence should be integrated into current
   new learning models.},
