Abstract = {The aim of this article is to highlight the role of consumer's goals, in
   this case the ``health{''} goal, in the cognitive representations and
   perception of food products, in particular ``health foods.{''} On the
   basis of the goal theories used in a categorical approach in information
   processing, we show that the salience of health goals has a significant
   influence on the perceived typicality of the products in the health food
   category. The consumption context and the overall hierarchy of the goals
   sought constitute moderating variables.},
