   Univ; New York Acad Sci; European Soc Cognit Sci Music},
Abstract = {The general aim of this experiment was to investigate the processes
   involved in reading musical notation and to study the relationship
   between written music and its auditory representation. Our main interest
   was to determine if musicians can develop expectancies for plausible or
   implausible auditory events on the sole basis of the visual score.
   Results showed that musicians can clearly expect auditory endings on the
   basis of visual information. These findings enliven the discussion on
   the question of whether music reading is actually music perception.},
