   Processes, MARSEILLE, FRANCE, MAY 15-16, 1997},
Abstract = {Anticipatory behavior is based upon expectations about perceptions and
   actions which will take place in the near future. It is manifest in the
   sensory domain and in the motor domain. In order to be effective,
   anticipatory behavior has to be selective. Requin et al. (1991) have
   argued that the similar function of selection in attention and motor
   preparation suggests a common adaptive role in goal directed behavior.
   The present contribution suggests that this similarity in function is
   based upon a structural neuro-anatomical similarity.},
