   2024},
Abstract = {Majority water used in the construction, right from the manufacturing
   stage till execution of building construction happens with use of
   potable water. Depletion of water table, no proper means of recharging
   groundwater and scarcity of potable water is posing a major threat in
   urban areas. The current study aims at identifying the percentage use of
   water during various construction phases, replacement of potable water
   usage with secondary treated water and the applicability of blocks
   manufactured using secondary treated water. Cube Compressive strength of
   25 MPa blocks manufactured and cured using secondary treated water were
   found to be 1.2\% more than the conventional blocks cured under potable
   water at 28 days. This experimental research studying the performance of
   concrete blocks with treated water cured in treated water is one of the
   ways to address the reduced dependency on potable water.},
